  "text_input": "72-year-old male presented with a 3-day history of cough with mucoid expectoration and sudden onset breathlessness (MMRC Grade 4). Known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (4 years), Pancreatic Carcinoma (Stage IV) with hepatic and peritoneal metastasis (post 6 cycles chemotherapy), and Ischemic Heart Disease with Heart Failure. Examination revealed pallor, clubbing, bilateral rhonchi, and an ejection systolic murmur. Investigations showed Hemoglobin 8.9 g/dL, WBC 9610/\u00b5L, Platelets 379,000/\u00b5L, and ESR 37 mm/hr. 2D Echo indicated Dilated Cardiomyopathy with EF 35-40% and severe aortic stenosis. Diagnosed with Bronchopneumonia and acute exacerbation of heart failure. Treated with IV antibiotics (Veotaz, Claribid), insulin, and cardiac medications. Referred to a higher center for cardiac intervention (AVR/Angiography).",
